title: loop3_research_wing_on_enter
---
<<if not $loop3_opening_seen>>
    <<jump loop3_opening>>
<<endif>>
===

title: loop3_opening
---
Narrator: The floor again. The ringing. The light is worse this time — something in the wall cracked between then and now, and nobody caused it in this loop.
Orin: On your feet.
Doss: Door.
Narrator: He was already watching it.
Kaleo: I should note that I have run this calculation before —
Narrator: \[Drops. The suppression field is up.\]
<<set $loop3_opening_seen = true>>
===

title: loop3_research_wing_on_combat_end
---
<<if not $constancy_zealot_heard>>
    <<jump loop3_constancy_zealot_dying>>
<<endif>>
===

title: loop3_constancy_zealot_dying
---
Narrator: One Zealot is down but not dead. If you leave them, they speak before the end.
Zealot: You think we're wrong.
Narrator: Not an accusation. A statement.
Zealot: You'll understand why we came. Before the end.
<<set $constancy_zealot_heard = true>>
===

title: loop3_command_deck_on_enter
---
<<if $companion == "orin" and $companion_orin and not $loop3_post_split_orin_seen>>
    <<jump loop3_post_split_orin>>
<<endif>>
===

title: loop3_post_split_orin
---
Orin: The anomaly is worse than it should be at the start of a loop. You'll see that in the readings.
Narrator: She said 'start of a loop' without pausing.
<<set $loop3_post_split_orin_seen = true>>
-> You said 'start of a loop.'
    <<jump loop3_orin_slip_caught>>
-> \[Let it pass.\]
===

title: loop3_orin_slip_caught
---
Orin: I meant start of a — the start of this situation. The crisis.
Narrator: The correction is smooth. It should feel reassuring. It doesn't.
===

title: loop3_command_deck_on_interact
---
<<if $companion == "orin" and $companion_orin and not $orin_logs_partial>>
    <<jump loop3_orin_logs_access>>
<<endif>>
===

title: loop3_orin_logs_access
---
Orin: Some of it isn't — I'm not ready to show you all of it yet.
Narrator: She says 'yet' like she means it. You don't know if she does.
Narrator: She opens a partial log. Entries from before the loop began — her voice, clipped and precise, documenting anomaly readings. Then a gap. Then entries that begin mid-sentence, as though she started recording and thought better of it.
<<set $orin_logs_partial = true>>
-> What's in the gap?
    <<jump loop3_orin_logs_gap>>
-> \[Read what she's shown you.\]
===

title: loop3_orin_logs_gap
---
Orin: Personal notes. Not relevant to the mission.
Narrator: She closes the terminal.
===

title: loop3_military_annex_on_enter
---
<<if $kaleo_recruited and not $loop3_kaleo_first_warning_seen>>
    <<jump loop3_kaleo_first_warning>>
<<endif>>
===

title: loop3_kaleo_first_warning
---
Kaleo: There are two Security Units in the next room. They have been aggressive since loop — since their last maintenance cycle.
Narrator: You hadn't asked.
<<set $loop3_kaleo_first_warning_seen = true>>
-> How did you know that?
    <<jump loop3_kaleo_first_evasion>>
-> \[Proceed with the warning in mind.\]
===

title: loop3_kaleo_first_evasion
---
Kaleo: I have access to the station's sensor grid.
Narrator: A beat.
Kaleo: That is the accurate answer.
<<set $kaleo_knows_more = true>>
===

title: loop3_military_annex_on_interact
---
<<if $companion == "doss" and $companion_doss and not $doss_bunk_found>>
    <<jump loop3_doss_bunk>>
<<elseif $doss_bunk_found and not $doss_war_referenced and not $loop3_doss_oblique_seen>>
    <<jump loop3_doss_war_oblique_no_companion>>
<<endif>>
===

title: loop3_doss_bunk
---
Narrator: Maps on the bunk. Tactical maps — grid references, force positions, supply lines. You pull up the location index and find nothing. These places don't exist in any database you can reach.
Doss: Old habit.
Narrator: He's in the doorway. He doesn't ask how you found them.
Doss: Sit down.
Narrator: He sits on the edge of the bunk. Doesn't look at you.
Doss: You ever been in something you couldn't walk away from? Not because they stopped you. Because walking away meant it happened for nothing.
<<set $doss_bunk_found = true>>
-> What happened?
    <<jump loop3_doss_war_not_yet>>
-> What are those maps of?
    <<jump loop3_doss_maps_question>>
-> \[Say nothing.\]
    <<jump loop3_doss_bunk_silence>>
===

title: loop3_doss_war_not_yet
---
Doss: Not yet.
===

title: loop3_doss_maps_question
---
Doss: A place I was. A long time ago.
Doss: Doesn't matter where. Matters what happened there.
<<set $doss_war_referenced = true>>
===

title: loop3_doss_bunk_silence
---
Doss: Good answer.
===

title: loop3_doss_war_oblique_no_companion
---
Doss: You're Orin's, aren't you.
Narrator: Not a question.
Doss: There was a war. She thinks she knows what it means. She doesn't.
Narrator: He doesn't elaborate. He goes back to cleaning his rifle.
<<set $doss_war_referenced = true>>
<<set $loop3_doss_oblique_seen = true>>
===

title: loop3_docking_bay_gun_for_hire_on_interact
---
<<if not $gfh_docking_loop3_seen>>
    <<jump loop3_gfh>>
<<endif>>
===

title: loop3_gfh
---
GunForHire: You want to know if I'm still selling intel.
Narrator: He says it before you can ask. Not a trick — he's been thinking about it.
GunForHire: I am. But I want something real. Not credit. Not favors. Passage confirmation — get me on whatever's leaving this station, if anything is.
<<set $gfh_docking_loop3_seen = true>>
-> I can't promise that.
    <<jump loop3_gfh_no_promise>>
-> What do you know?
    <<jump loop3_gfh_intel>>
===

title: loop3_gfh_no_promise
---
GunForHire: Then we're both being honest.
Narrator: He leans against the wall.
GunForHire: Here's what I'll tell you for free: Doss has been talking to my crew. Don't know what he's promising them, but they're listening.
===

title: loop3_gfh_intel
---
GunForHire: Drifter Boss has set up in the Relay Array. That's their command position — which means anything you do there is going to draw response from here.
GunForHire: And the Constancy moved deeper. Past the Research Wing. Whatever they came for, they think it's in the Core.
===

title: loop3_medical_bay_salvage_operative_on_interact
---
<<if not $med_salvage_op_loop3_seen>>
    <<jump loop3_med_salvage_op>>
<<endif>>
===

title: loop3_med_salvage_op
---
SalvageOperative: I'm not selling anymore. What I have, I'm keeping.
Narrator: She says it flat. Not hostile — decided.
<<set $med_salvage_op_loop3_seen = true>>
-> Something happened.
    <<jump loop3_med_salvage_op_what_happened>>
-> \[Respect it and go.\]
===

title: loop3_med_salvage_op_what_happened
---
SalvageOperative: The other operative who was working this wing — she was here yesterday. She's not here now and I can't reach her and I can't explain where the time went between when I last saw her and now.
Narrator: A long pause.
SalvageOperative: I'm keeping my supplies.
===

title: loop3_station_exterior_salvage_operative_on_interact
---
<<if not $exterior_salvage_op_loop3_seen>>
    <<jump loop3_exterior_salvage_op>>
<<endif>>
===

title: loop3_exterior_salvage_op
---
Narrator: She's alone on the surface. The only figure in a lot of open ground.
SalvageOperative: Good. I've been waiting for someone with authority to move through here.
Narrator: You don't tell her you don't have authority.
SalvageOperative: I have supplies and I have a working ship docked at the secondary port. I want confirmation that I'm cleared to leave. That's the trade.
<<set $exterior_salvage_op_loop3_seen = true>>
-> I can't clear your departure.
    <<jump loop3_exterior_salvage_op_no_clearance>>
-> What supplies?
    <<jump loop3_exterior_salvage_op_supplies>>
===

title: loop3_exterior_salvage_op_no_clearance
---
SalvageOperative: Then what can you give me?
Narrator: It's a genuine question. She's been out here calculating trades for long enough that she's down to the honest ones.
-> Intel on the station interior.
    <<jump loop3_exterior_salvage_op_intel_trade>>
-> Nothing. I'm sorry.
    <<jump loop3_exterior_salvage_op_nothing>>
===

title: loop3_exterior_salvage_op_intel_trade
---
SalvageOperative: That's something.
Narrator: She takes what you have. She gives you what she has. The exchange is quick and professional.
SalvageOperative: The Relay Array has had signal activity in a direction that doesn't correspond to any logged installation. Started three days ago.
SalvageOperative: I don't know what that means. Maybe you do.
===

title: loop3_exterior_salvage_op_nothing
---
SalvageOperative: Yeah.
Narrator: She looks back at the horizon. The dying star is very large from out here.
===

title: loop3_exterior_salvage_op_supplies
---
SalvageOperative: Medical consumables, two portable power cells, and one environment suit that's missing its left glove.
SalvageOperative: The suit's still good for thirty minutes outside if you don't mind a slow leak.
===

title: loop3_systems_core_on_interact
---
Kaleo: I said what I meant.
Kaleo: I would be more useful in the field.
Narrator: The terminal waits. The offer stands.
===

title: loop3_systems_core_on_enter
---
<<if not $kaleo_recruited>>
    <<jump loop3_kaleo_recruitment>>
<<endif>>
===

title: loop3_kaleo_recruitment
---
Narrator: The terminal displays a single line: UNIT KALEO — I WOULD BE MORE USEFUL IN THE FIELD.
Narrator: It appeared once. It is waiting.
-> \[Accept.\]
    <<set $kaleo_recruited = true>>
    <<set $companion = "kaleo">>
    <<jump loop3_kaleo_joins>>
-> \[Ignore it and move on.\]
===

title: loop3_kaleo_joins
---
Narrator: The terminal goes dark. A moment later, Kaleo's voice comes from the corridor speaker — closer than a station-wide broadcast should sound.
Kaleo: Thank you. I will try not to be an inconvenience.
===
